{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":47,"timestamp":"2026-07-11T20:11:58.728409190Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"d691bf6c-5bf6-47f0-a0ca-d64fb76b0695","title":"psptool-core: follow tertiary (0x48/0x4A) L2 directory pointers — Zen 4 double-indirection","description":"Steps to reproduce:\n1. \n\nExpected: \nActual: \n\nDiscovered by differential testing against freshly collected Zen 4/5 AM5 firmware (3 ASRock ROMs; see below). psptool-rs discovers NONE of the real firmware directories on modern AM5 images — it reports only the L1 `$PSP` stub(s), while reference PSPTool reports 4 (B650) / 8 (X870E, B850).\n\n## Root cause\nModern AM5 firmware nests its real L2 directories behind **tertiary pointer entries** (types `0x48 PSP_FW_L2A_PTR` / `0x4A PSP_FW_L2B_PTR`). Our L1 `$PSP` directory parses to exactly two entries of these types and stops. `crates/psptool-core/src/directory.rs:559` documents this as a deliberate gap: \"Tertiary pointers (entry types 0x48 / 0x4A — §3.3) are *not* followed.\"\n\nReference resolves them with a **double indirection introduced in Zen 4** (`/tmp/psptool-ref/psptool/directory.py:85-99`):\n1. read 32 bytes at the 0x48/0x4A entry file_offset;\n2. `actual_offset = le_u32(body[16:20])` — the real L2 directory address lives INSIDE the pointer block;\n3. `zen_generation_id = body[21:24]` (and full id `le_u32(body[20:24])`) — this is the source of the `Unknown zen_generation_id=...` warnings;\n4. recurse into `actual_offset` via `create_directories_if_not_exist`.\n\nType tables (`/tmp/psptool-ref/psptool/file.py:34-35`): SECONDARY = [0x40,0x49,0x70] (already followed by us), TERTIARY = [0x48,0x4a] (NOT followed).\n\n## Impact\nBlocks ALL directory/entry discovery on Zen 4/5 consumer AM5 firmware. The Zen 1-3 corpus never exercised the tertiary path, so this was invisible until now. `corpus_roundtrip` still passes (we emit unparsed bytes unchanged → trivially byte-exact), masking the gap; only `differential` catches it.\n\n## New generation IDs\nThe 2026 X870E/B850 v4.43 images carry PSP generation IDs newer than reference PSPTool 3.6 knows: `0xbc0e0b` and `0xbc0e10` (reference emits `Unknown zen_generation_id`). psptool-rs must reproduce the same \"unknown\" fallback for differential parity.\n\n## Repro\nSupplementary corpus (gitignored, machine-local): /tmp/psp-extra/supp-corpus/test_files/\n  - ASRock_B650_PG_Lightning_1.14.AS06[Beta].bin  (gen 0xbc0d0300, 4 dirs)\n  - ASRock_X870E_Taichi_4.43.bin                   (gen 0xbc0e0b/0xbc0e10, 8 dirs)\n  - ASRock_B850_Steel_Legend_WiFi_4.43.bin         (gen 0xbc0e0b/0xbc0e10, 8 dirs)\nRun: PSPTOOL_TEST_CORPUS=/tmp/psp-extra/supp-corpus cargo test -p psptool-cli --test differential\n\n## Fix sketch\nExtend directory recursion to follow TERTIARY types with the +16 offset / +20..24 gen-id double-indirection, mirroring directory.py:85-99. Belongs to the fet.rs/directory.rs translation unit. A minimal committed micro-fixture (L1 dir + 32-byte tertiary block + tiny L2 dir) should pin it durably, since the full ROMs are 32MB each and cannot live in the repo.","priority":"high","parent_uuid":"525d7258-de71-4087-8d5a-f7dd155266b5","created_by":"tLiK"},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBDZbFWzW7zq7KjlEFYN2Hr9R66HYn/Gh3TQosn0ocGO26icgWzH6LFF0c9CNNT/0GkHUxFwnsQ/ARuaMczonwE="}
