{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":50,"timestamp":"2026-07-11T21:17:45.915685333Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"d691bf6c-5bf6-47f0-a0ca-d64fb76b0695","comment_uuid":"678a9d58-7e67-4e81-8a51-385f55a01a47","author":"tLiK","content":"Empirical byte-level confirmation from ASRock_B650_PG_Lightning (gen 0xbc0d0300), ready-to-drop micro-fixture spec.\n\nL1 `$PSP` directory @ 0x81000, count=2, both entries tertiary:\n\n```\nentry0: type=0x48 location=0x83020\n  tertiary block @0x83020 (32B): 758e6a37 ffffffff 0f000000 00ffffff 00d05700 00030dbc ffffffff ffffffff\n    actual_offset = le_u32(block[16:20]) = 0x57d000\n    gen_id        = le_u32(block[20:24]) = 0xbc0d0300\n    -> L2 dir @0x57d000: magic $PL2, count=38\nentry1: type=0x4a location=0x84000\n  tertiary block @0x84000 (32B): 2a8e6b35 02000000 0f000000 00ffffff 00d00a00 00030dbc ffffffff ffffffff\n    actual_offset = le_u32(block[16:20]) = 0xad000\n    gen_id        = le_u32(block[20:24]) = 0xbc0d0300\n    -> L2 dir @0xad000: magic $PL2, count=38\n```\n\nThis matches directory.py:85-99 exactly. Reference reports 4 dirs for B650 = the 2 tertiary targets (0x57d000, 0xad000) + 2 secondary continuations (0x2ed000, 0x7bd000) reachable via 0x40/0x49/0x70 entries WITHIN those $PL2 dirs (which we already follow). So implementing ONLY the tertiary double-indirection should close the full gap.\n\nMicro-fixture recipe (no 32MB ROM needed): synthesize an L1 $PSP dir with one 0x48 entry whose location points at a 32-byte block with actual_offset at +16 and gen_id at +20, targeting a tiny 1-entry $PL2 dir. Assert the parser surfaces the $PL2 dir at actual_offset. Add under crates/psptool-fixtures/data/ + a directory.rs unit test. Also cover the unknown-gen case: X870E/B850 blocks carry gen_id 0xbc0e0b/0xbc0e10 which must map to an \"unknown\" classification without erroring (matches reference `Unknown zen_generation_id` warning path).","created_at":"2026-07-11T21:17:45.876985256Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAEqLDVT8ErnhpNXHKWGfaLkiiNz5Vf10W4w+fD7JPup6RjxLcJ3VNB3Hi1d/Dq/r/5VBjng/zO+L8Wdl/cWW7CQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQN4WMrlut4MpCMdnSNmr0DpNrnL9wUqkIgtXh5da0Xv45f40aDfH232lYmc/109Yn+W+L5S/smY8BsUc1TqUfgY="}
{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":51,"timestamp":"2026-07-11T21:45:38.365363333Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"e5722ead-8cd4-4006-8598-6cb24d15adbd","title":"psptool-core: entry address-mode divergence on upper-half (>16MB) directories — SP5 EPYC","description":"Steps to reproduce:\n1. \n\nExpected: \nActual: \n\nFound by differential testing against SP5 EPYC firmware (ASRockRack GENOAD8HM3 Zen4 Genoa + TURIND12M3-2QE810 Zen5 Turin). BOTH fail identically — server firmware parses past the #51 tertiary-pointer wall (secondary dirs work) but diverges on entry address computation.\n\n## Symptom\n`directory @0x1332000, entry 11`:\n  ours:      address 0x13c8000, size 0x3800, type TEE_BOOT_DRIVER~0x1b\n  reference: address 0x3c8000,  size 0x30,   type WRAPPED_IKEK~0x21\n\n## Byte-level root cause (GENOAD8HM3)\ndir @0x1332000 = magic $PL2, count=48, PSP directory (16B entries), in the UPPER 16MB half of the 32MB ROM.\nRaw entry 11 record (PSP 16B stride): type=0x1b, size=0x3800, loc=0x3c8000.\n- OUR parse: type/size match the raw record, but address = 0x13c8000 = (raw loc 0x3c8000 | 0x1000000). We spuriously OR bit 24 (the directory region base) into an entry whose loc points to the LOWER half.\n- REFERENCE parse: address = 0x3c8000 (raw loc, unbiased).\n\nThis is an address-mode / addr_mask application bug: for a directory located in the upper 16MB, we bias entry addresses into the upper half instead of honoring the entry loc field/address-mode bits. PSP entry address fields carry mode bits (top bits) selecting relative-to-ROM vs relative-to-directory; reference honors them (see entry.py / directory.py address handling), we do not for this case.\n\nSecondary symptom: reference reports entry 11 type=0x21/size=0x30 (differs from raw slot 11) — reference flattens secondary-directory continuation entries into one list, shifting its index vs our per-directory index. Track the address-mode bug as primary here; the index-alignment nuance is for the differential harness comparison layer.\n\n## Belongs to\naddress.rs translation unit (route already seeded in tooling/translate-routes.toml; upstream entry.py + directory.py). Distinct from #51 (directory.rs tertiary pointers).\n\n## Repro\nPSPTOOL_TEST_CORPUS=/tmp/psp-extra/epyc-corpus cargo test -p psptool-cli --test differential\n(images preserved in gitignored .local-corpus/test_files/: ASRockRack_GENOAD8HM3_11.01.bin, ASRockRack_TURIND12M3-2QE810_10.05.bin)\n\nroundtrip PASSES (unmodified bytes emitted verbatim); only differential catches it.","priority":"high","parent_uuid":"525d7258-de71-4087-8d5a-f7dd155266b5","created_by":"tLiK"},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCnxaBfPuaT7atKgVTHx6VyVPoDDetLXps49Jq0ilJevFEbfspSlhEveYT79uaaBJz89+ghT47lEJEzEtBGcYw0="}
