{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":54,"timestamp":"2026-07-11T21:54:17.549493258Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"d691bf6c-5bf6-47f0-a0ca-d64fb76b0695","comment_uuid":"f9d17d44-1a58-4625-baec-40c09fcad1f4","author":"tLiK","content":"Failing test pin committed: crates/psptool-core/tests/divergence_tertiary.rs::{divergence_tertiary_0x48_known_gen_surfaces_l2, divergence_tertiary_0x4a_unknown_gen_still_surfaces_l2}. Both build a minimal L1 $PSP -> 32B tertiary block -> L2 $PL2 chain and assert walk_directories surfaces the $PL2 at block[16:20]. Both FAIL today (only the L1 $PSP is surfaced; surfaced dirs = [(\"$PSP\", 0x30000)]) for the right reason: the walk continues past 0x48/0x4A entries per directory.rs:657-661. Control assertion confirms the L1 stub IS reached, so the failure is specifically the tertiary miss, not a broken fixture. Marked #[ignore] with tracking note per R-DEFER-3; run with 'cargo test -p psptool-core --test divergence_tertiary -- --include-ignored'. Mirrors upstream directory.py:85-99.","created_at":"2026-07-11T21:54:17.544536891Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAWsa9lI9Fun5PPHnKSnlvJeQrcJ6nAiRyznTT+uyaQp0TiQBK4ZA+zF+b3zsZjq2ddNKYhBqJUbRX78DJIBXFAA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOZNPKrs8s9WjrDHFDFt2QKfIu2bn3az+IGDZOWQuBF+RC5t8NzE5aEpiPtn/iKj6RQ4ahH+OF2UN1w0sTeDkgI="}
{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":55,"timestamp":"2026-07-11T21:55:25.099353310Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"4438c167-6f65-469f-9ff4-a0773b7edddf","title":"upstream-parity: manual ROM-size/offset override for embedded images (PSPTool #19)","description":"Upstream: https://github.com/PSPReverse/PSPTool/issues/19 (also #26). Open/declined-unshipped.\n\nWhen the PSP ROM is embedded in a larger container (bootable-CD ISO, UEFI capsule, memory dump spanning two mmap windows), file size != ROM size, so our 'largest power-of-two <= blob_len' heuristic in fet.rs::detect_rom_layout picks the wrong addr mask and every physical address mis-resolves -> total misparse (correctness).\n\nUpstream endorsed 'assume a default and provide an option to manually specify the UEFI image size' but never shipped it.\n\nImpl: thread a caller-supplied rom_size/rom_origin override into detect_rom_layout (skip heuristic when set); add --rom-size/--rom-offset flags in crates/psptool-cli/src/cli.rs. Roundtrip-safe (only affects masking). See docs/upstream-issue-review.md.","priority":"medium","parent_uuid":"525d7258-de71-4087-8d5a-f7dd155266b5","created_by":"tLiK"},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFg8Sc+FZyuVU3j6t83Sp/kk0iHJuhdA0BK/m6Rzrjy1Nr4BEXm9flJhDD24kQRVB102FDYkxLR2l5irWIMy6Qw="}
