{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":57,"timestamp":"2026-07-11T21:55:35.384219290Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"d434f175-a545-41e6-9748-d52c77e1eb5d","title":"upstream-parity: resolve inline pubkeys in verify (same-ID-as-file) (PSPTool #51)","description":"Upstream: https://github.com/PSPReverse/PSPTool/issues/51 -- OPEN, confirmed regression (bisected to 0bda1bd). Maintainer memo: 'inline keys that happen to have the same ID as the file itself are not shown', so their signed entries show key_missing instead of verified.\n\npsptool-rs risk: crates/psptool-ops/src/verify.rs builds its key_id->pubkey map from STRUCTURED directory pubkey entries only, while inline keys are discovered separately by the heuristic scan in search_keys.rs (try_heuristic_at). A signature signed by an inline-only key can therefore surface as key_missing -- same failure class. Translating upstream as-is inherits the bug.\n\nImpl: feed heuristic/inline pubkey hits into the verify key map (or make search_keys_with_directories the single key source); ensure a key whose key_id == containing file's own ID is not filtered. Add a fixture whose only signer is an inline key. See docs/upstream-issue-review.md.","priority":"medium","parent_uuid":"525d7258-de71-4087-8d5a-f7dd155266b5","created_by":"tLiK"},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEY4N7WwovwuI7n/FzO9yZvbr2AjaXOvIeUTfsWr81zZaZ/JBrCeoBdgvtdMtrUGQzBUshvM0LnpOajPDn4/XAU="}
