{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":59,"timestamp":"2026-07-11T21:55:48.199825198Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"15eeff8e-9c99-40c2-bed4-ce9bcd171d18","title":"upstream-parity: back-fill zen_generation for single-gen EPYC BIOSes (PSPTool #85)","description":"Upstream PR: https://github.com/PSPReverse/PSPTool/pull/85 -- OPEN.\n\nEPYC server BIOSes (Naples-Turin) use single-FET -> single $PSP + $BHD. Neither combo_dir nor tertiary self-tag detection fires, so every directory/entry returns zen_generation=None SILENTLY; downstream tooling that bins by generation drops these rows.\n\nFix (from PR#85): when a ROM's directories are uniformly unclassified, read PSP_FW_BOOT_LOADER (entry type 0x01) version major and map via BOOTLOADER_VERSION_TO_ZEN (Naples->Turin), applying to all dirs incl $BHD. Conservative: only fires when every dir is None; warn on unknown bootloader version.\n\nDistinct from crosslink #52 (that is entry ADDRESS-MODE on upper-half dirs, not generation labeling).\n\nImpl: crates/psptool-core/src/directory.rs generation detection. Version major at version[1] for a Rome bootloader -- verify byte order vs body.rs. See docs/upstream-issue-review.md.","priority":"medium","parent_uuid":"525d7258-de71-4087-8d5a-f7dd155266b5","created_by":"tLiK"},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMUMcio3KselwrPEj0yAhbmVIz6MOi7hKIZd5QyFWyLowF50GvLo4omrvgTazbPw52G9lqTAHpxJAe6zvOrU2Q4="}
