{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":61,"timestamp":"2026-07-11T21:56:14.217817789Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"7c5ec29a-d96d-4643-89c6-90b347dcfe44","title":"upstream-parity: surface parse warnings + optional --strict mode (PSPTool #38)","description":"Upstream: https://github.com/PSPReverse/PSPTool/issues/38 (reinforced by closed PR#31 https://github.com/PSPReverse/PSPTool/pull/31). OPEN.\n\nUpstream prints 'Warning: ...' for every entry/directory it can't parse and continues; #38 additionally wants a strict mode (assert) for scientific work and a very-lenient mode for reconstructed/partial ROMs.\n\npsptool-rs already continues past unparseable records (directory.rs Err(_) => continue at ~608/634/660/691) but SILENTLY. That is a differential-parity gap (upstream emits those warnings to stderr; we don't) and hurts diagnosability of exactly the crash issues in this review (#57/#60/#63/#66 were all 'warned then crashed' upstream). A collected warning list also enables --strict to escalate skips to hard errors.\n\nImpl: thread a warning sink through the directory/entry walk (crates/psptool-core/src/directory.rs, entry.rs) returning (parsed, Vec<ParseWarning>); render to stderr in CLI; add --strict. Happy-path roundtrip unchanged. See docs/upstream-issue-review.md.","priority":"low","parent_uuid":"525d7258-de71-4087-8d5a-f7dd155266b5","created_by":"tLiK"},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQME6dfeCD4104XPBB0r2OQ2CDYMcO7WlM+v/B+fcuVU/F6zKC1y9TqXSdWInpAiRF/guoFBWUTrqsqUDZZWARAA="}
