{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":65,"timestamp":"2026-07-11T21:56:37.326025901Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"a0d69506-28e3-43b3-9b3d-69c6c1bbf081","title":"upstream-parity: deduplicate entries referenced by multiple directories for mutation correctness (PSPTool #37)","description":"Upstream: https://github.com/PSPReverse/PSPTool/issues/37 -- OPEN.\n\nOne physical region (start+size) can be pointed at by multiple directory entries across directories (upstream keeps a Rom.unique_entries set).\n\npsptool-rs mutation risk: replace patches by flash offset, but each directory RECORD's size field is a separate location. If two records reference the same region, replace must update BOTH records (and both fletcher checksums) or the second directory keeps a stale size -> corrupt roundtrip. A parse-time cross-reference index makes this correct and detectable.\n\nImpl: build a flash_offset -> Vec<EntryRef> index during the directory walk (crates/psptool-core/src/directory.rs), consumed by crates/psptool-ops/src/replace.rs so a size change fans out to every referencing record. See docs/upstream-issue-review.md.","priority":"low","parent_uuid":"525d7258-de71-4087-8d5a-f7dd155266b5","created_by":"tLiK"},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJSPCzTpfiy7Itb8lypoTRdunLA+yJ5FyyH5mA4OH2G0cZO34BRZKqVRWMBgo5pN7RhqqaJV8eQMQTH5nxMQlAU="}
