{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":85,"timestamp":"2026-07-11T23:10:40.040225970Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"a6322983-624f-4612-bcad-795481ee0f8d","title":"Version skew: differential oracle (psptool 3.4) != translation source (git HEAD ~3.6) — needs alignment decision","description":"Steps to reproduce:\n1. \n\nExpected: \nActual: \n\nFOUNDATION ISSUE surfaced while triaging #60. The two \"reference PSPTool\" endpoints are DIFFERENT VERSIONS:\n\n- Differential ORACLE: default.nix:38-53 pins `referencePsptool` to PyPI **psptool 3.4** (HATCH_VCS_PRETEND_VERSION=3.4), consumed as PSPTOOL_REFERENCE by crates/psptool-cli/tests/differential.rs. Deliberate, documented (\"pinned PyPI sdist keeps the reference reproducible\").\n- Translation SOURCE: goal.md / memory clone `/tmp/psptool-ref` via `git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/PSPReverse/PSPTool` = **git HEAD (~3.6)**.\n\nBetween 3.4 and HEAD, PSPTool changed things. Confirmed example (issue #60): entry type 0x5c renamed `WMOS` (3.4, file.py:149) -> `SPI_ROM_CONFIG` (HEAD, file.py:149). Our Rust matches HEAD (SPI_ROM_CONFIG); the 3.4 oracle says WMOS; so AORUS_X570 + the 3 AM5 local images \"fail\" differential on a NON-bug. Any type-name-map or behavior change between 3.4 and HEAD produces the same false divergence. This undermines the differential contract wherever the versions diverge.\n\nDECISION NEEDED (which version is authoritative?):\n(A) Pin BOTH to the SAME explicit version/rev (RECOMMENDED). Either:\n    (A1) bump the oracle to the same tag/rev as the translation source (translate + test against newest, pin the rev for reproducibility), or\n    (A2) pin /tmp/psptool-ref to the 3.4 release tag to match the deliberately-pinned oracle (keeps citations stable-ish, loses newest improvements).\n(B) Keep both versions and add a differential tolerance layer for known cross-version renames (fragile; not recommended).\n\nIMPACT: already-translated units (fletcher/entry/directory/entry-taxonomy) cited git-HEAD line numbers; option A2 may shift some citations. #60 and future type-map divergences are BLOCKED on this decision — do NOT \"fix\" them by editing our type map until the authoritative version is chosen, or we risk regressing to match a stale oracle.\n\nUntil resolved: the committed corpus differential is GREEN (our translations happen to match 3.4 there), so this only bites on newer/renamed surfaces. Recommend the user pick A1 or A2 in the morning.","priority":"high","parent_uuid":"525d7258-de71-4087-8d5a-f7dd155266b5","created_by":"tLiK"},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQA8VRwdet0cScAha3j++HZXcpCWnpE8WiAW7sy4ln7tMZNpHLicMtiAOKpoqYGHYPdE4W9Qml3ZQydKVPX4rfQI="}
