{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":112,"timestamp":"2026-07-11T23:49:07.068932888Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"71fbd789-f59a-4c42-aaf0-37ff9463e9c0","comment_uuid":"6614f5c7-16e3-44eb-a921-19de2af6a658","author":"tLiK","content":"Failing test at crates/psptool-ops/tests/divergence_fletcher.rs:length_changing_replace_recomputes_directory_checksum demonstrates the divergence (stored 0x15190283 stale vs recomputed 0x14cb0276 after a 0x40->0x33 shrink). Control equal_length_replace_keeps_directory_checksum_valid passes, isolating the changed size field as the cause. Fix belongs in crates/psptool-ops/src/replace.rs::apply — after rewrite_size_field, recompute fletcher32 over the parent directory's [0x08..header+table] region and patch the checksum field at record-dir +0x04. Deferral in replace.rs:34-39 pointed at #13, which is CLOSED (R-DEFER-3). writer.rs itself is byte-exact-correct; this is a consumer-side omission surfaced by the writer audit.","created_at":"2026-07-11T23:49:07.064317435Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAoWBzy5q7o7fyVmgDumTtsGIavRq8ai/sresevQvKYEQ1xhD2TBTAruHdfFQC1bhG5LyKnxR9gkmRrbrznPtMDw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJ30zlVUXgZ6TF7S+aL6YXGD8apT3fBAdNFXNFJgY8XheNfQz5M/+ELBUsuCsBOQAQtYo25RWw/PkZ0ncOK4tg8="}
{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":113,"timestamp":"2026-07-11T23:53:35.502475238Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"71fbd789-f59a-4c42-aaf0-37ff9463e9c0","comment_uuid":"bb80da7b-6ade-4b7b-bdaf-19fbcf360ab5","author":"tLiK","content":"PLAN (acto-fixer, #66 length-changing replace leaves directory fletcher32 stale):\n\nEDIT SITE: crates/psptool-ops/src/replace.rs::apply (~142), plus the two family entry-points that hold the parent directory (replace_psp_entry_body/replace_bios_entry_body) and the stale defer note (34-39).\n\nWHY UPSTREAM RECOMPUTES: On --replace-file, directory.update_entry_fields (directory.py:207) writes entry.size (entry.py:109-110 -> set_bytes(4,4,...)) then calls update_checksum() UNCONDITIONALLY (directory.py:241). update_checksum (directory.py:203-205) does data=self[0x8:]; checksum.set_bytes(0,4,fletcher32(data)) — self[0x8:] is header[8:] ++ entry table (directory.py:132-134), and the fresh Fletcher-32 lands in the header checksum field at [0x04..0x08] (self.checksum=NestedBuffer(self,4,4), directory.py:135).\n\nREASONING CHAIN -> EDIT: the size field the replace rewrites (replace.rs:rewrite_size_field, record+0x04) lands inside the checksummed region. So after rewrite_size_field + body patch, recompute fletcher32 over the POST-replace directory bytes [0x08 .. end-of-entry-table] and patch the 4-byte LE result at dir_base+0x04. The checksummed region is exactly PspDirectory/BiosDirectory.source (header+entry table); its base+0x08 == dir_base+0x08. Post-replace bytes = dir.source bytes with the new size u32 overlaid at (record_off-dir_base)+0x04 (the only mutation inside the region; the body patch is outside it).\n\nMECHANICS: thread the directory source into apply as Option<&SourceBytes> (Some(&parent.source) for the two family fns used by the CLI + the pin; None for the entry-only replace_entry_body which structurally lacks the parent). Use the fallible psptool_core::fletcher32 (Result, #45) -> new ReplaceError::Checksum(FletcherError) via thiserror; no unwrap/expect/panic (R-CODE-2), no truncating casts (R-CODE-5), only the checksum + already-patched size/body touched (R-CODE-4). Gate on length-change (equal-length leaves the size field + region byte-identical, so the control test + patch_count==1 stay green). Replace the stale replace.rs:34-39 defer-to-#13 note. Un-ignore length_changing_replace_recomputes_directory_checksum. Closes #66; gives fletcher32 its first production consumer (#43).","created_at":"2026-07-11T23:53:35.497861332Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA+K3wiLKy7Qgg7H7X0eci1cyGN+rkP5x0ro6YzIgb5isV0BYVCmgr/r8JOPh0+SgXeRqNQzjUxintQURAwTBXDg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLHpONZDRucReP7aSdWYUoyGc1zYe4Sb4oCiLM+ltR2BLZvcJ7q0eOHo/zskzzZuKt7pjKKJfGjWvtVR66BnwQQ="}
{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":114,"timestamp":"2026-07-11T23:55:48.808230358Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"71fbd789-f59a-4c42-aaf0-37ff9463e9c0","comment_uuid":"412fc547-2dbf-4dbc-ac9d-12b6ae41fa96","author":"tLiK","content":"BLOCKED (acto-fixer): fix scope exceeds single file; needs orchestrator-level coordination.\n\nThe minimal fix for #66 is fully specified (see the prior --kind plan comment) and the pin is confirmed RED (length_changing_replace_recomputes_directory_checksum panics at divergence_fletcher.rs:111). BUT the edit to crates/psptool-ops/src/replace.rs is HARD-BLOCKED by the translate-discipline read-gate:\n\n  translate-discipline: no route table entry matches 'crates/psptool-ops/src/replace.rs'.\n\nRoot cause: psptool-ops has NOT yet entered the 8-step loop. There is:\n  - NO route for crates/psptool-ops/src/replace.rs in tooling/translate-routes.toml (routes stop at psptool-core/writer.rs), and\n  - NO design doc .design/psptool-ops/replace.md (the .design/psptool-ops/ directory does not exist at all).\n\nPer goal.md R-XLATE-2 (routeless files are blocked) and R-XLATE-3 (a route whose design doc is missing blocks until acto-doc-author authors it), and the acto-fixer spec (R-FIX-3 single-file scope; 'design doc → doc-author'), this is out of acto-fixer scope. I did NOT circumvent the gate and made NO edits (working tree clean apart from pre-existing vendor/test-corpus + .worktrees).\n\nREQUIRED ORCHESTRATOR COORDINATION before re-dispatching the fixer:\n  1. Dispatch acto-doc-author to author .design/psptool-ops/replace.md grounded in crates/psptool-ops/src/replace.rs + upstream directory.py (update_entry_fields/update_checksum :203-241) + entry.py (:109-110 size setter) + __main__.py (:247 --replace-file). Include a REQ for 'length-changing replace recomputes the parent directory Fletcher-32' (the #66 fix) and one for fletcher32's production consumer (#43).\n  2. Add a [[route]] for crates/psptool-ops/src/replace.rs (upstream = directory.py, entry.py, __main__.py; design = .design/psptool-ops/replace.md; parity_ops = ['differential'] since the CLI replace path is differential-covered).\n  3. Re-dispatch acto-fixer for #66. The exact code change is already planned: thread parent.source into apply() as Option<&SourceBytes>, recompute fletcher32 over post-replace dir[0x08..end-of-entry-table] and patch LE at dir_base+0x04 (mirror directory.py:203-205), add ReplaceError::Checksum(#[from] FletcherError), gate on length-change, replace stale replace.rs:34-39 defer note, un-ignore the pin.\n\nLeaving #66 OPEN and #43 OPEN.","created_at":"2026-07-11T23:55:48.802330304Z","kind":"blocker","signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAYDdtTPSO4OOlXtGddTO96uS+h6uxKM+mioo+7t2344maKumayncwFBdn63w20Pi0C/JnEFOeoH/oVAGgVw0qCA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFYYoQp4ysyiItbtZ+KrCB967BcS+fHUi0UgbhGKMpS3TQAi40ZFUAz+mKot5NpAV6jUXr/LkBBiqdi2XEnvgwY="}
