{"agent_id":"tLiK","agent_seq":145,"timestamp":"2026-07-12T04:25:03.136035400Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"c3c8670f-9fe0-4508-8196-90362d7f2528","title":"psptool-ops: replace updates size+checksum only in the given parent directory, not every referencing directory (multi-ref divergence)","description":"Steps to reproduce:\n1. \n\nExpected: \nActual: \n\nSee HATER.md (committed) for the full adversarial analysis + failure scenario. Found by the-hater (Fable) review of the session's production changes. replace.rs:128-153 updates only the passed parent; upstream file.py:385-393 updates size+checksum in EVERY directory referencing the entry. For entries referenced by multiple dirs (multi-ROM), sibling records/checksums go stale. #41-multi-ROM family. Also: two family-API replaces in the SAME directory currently PatchError-overlap on the checksum field, and recompute_directory_checksum rebuilds from pristine dir_source (not editor post-patch state) so sequential same-dir replaces compose wrong. Upstream's live-buffer recompute handles all this. No production consumer does multi-replace-per-editor yet.","priority":"high","parent_uuid":"525d7258-de71-4087-8d5a-f7dd155266b5","created_by":"tLiK"},"signed_by":"SHA256:pi2rgM6dRaTX7StyiUVj9BegTQChW341Fra5MXz4iKc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOi3VkKr4Jd4JgqerRa/w7ChR2ooa2tu6OIM/yho/EaUAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFtVl82dWTgx4MKcSrF2waVniZtFyD/LJfi5qLKvfarqXRua2t6cHo2r/tug5j9LT36ls9Y47S26GsJS7WVOogg="}
